From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 03:52:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] settings: Extended memory on Kiln OS

Settings > System gets "Extended memory" under Return to Flashforge
firmware: on an AD5X with 512 MiB it gives Linux the whole memory from
the next start (Kiln OS uses 256 MiB by default, the same on every
AD5X). The state comes from Moonraker's kiln_os component
(machine.kiln_os.get_memory, GET /machine/kiln_os/memory), fetched in the
discovery sequence, so on every connect and Klipper restart; the row
shows only when the board has 512 MiB. Its switch posts the change
(machine.kiln_os.post_memory, POST /machine/kiln_os/memory with enable;
Kiln's update agent writes the switch) and is greyed while a job holds
the machine (kiln_power_locked). Moonraker names the JSON-RPC methods of
an endpoint with both GET and POST get_<name> and post_<name>.

After a change that needs a restart, "Restart now?" offers Restart,
which goes through Moonraker's machine.reboot as the Kiln power dialog
does (request_kiln_reboot: Kiln's update agent decides, a refusal is a
toast), or Later, which leaves it for the next start; the row then says
"Extended memory changes at the next start." A refused change puts the
switch back and shows Kiln's reason. One change at a time.

When Kiln says the one-time notice is due (notice_pending), it goes under
the bell once per run ("Extended memory available"); tapping it opens
Settings > System. Opening the bell (or clearing it) with the entry in it
tells Kiln it was seen (machine.kiln_os.memory_notice_seen), once, again
after a failed try. When a start with extended memory did not finish,
Kiln says why (failed): the row shows "Extended memory was turned off:
the printer didn't finish starting with it." with the switch off, and a
warning says the same once per failure (the failed text is kept in the
config).

When Kiln says a boot loader update is needed (bootloader_update_needed:
an older Kiln U-Boot started the printer and can't choose the mode, so a
restart changes nothing), the row shows the same switch with the
subtitle "Needs a boot loader update to take effect.", nothing is
pending, "Restart now?" is never asked and no notice goes under the bell.
The switch still posts the change; it counts after the update.

HELIX_KILN_AD5X builds only; elsewhere nothing is asked and the row stays
hidden. Strings in en and ru (the Russian notice is shorter, to fit the
bell entry's 255 bytes).

Tests: Kiln's object read field by field, when the switch and the
pending line show, the fetch filling the subjects, nothing asked off
Kiln or without a connection, an older Kiln without the method, switching
on (the POST, the restart prompt) and off (no prompt), a refusal, one
change at a time, a fetch during a change, no change before Kiln has
answered, the notice once and its seen once (again after a failure), a
failure once per failure, the bell marking the notice seen, a boot loader
update needed (its subtitle, the switch posting, no restart prompt, no
notice); the System page row's visibility, greying, switch, pending and
failure lines and the boot loader subtitle row.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
